The [page for #4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, known, one fix queued. Its own table
says otherwise. Run the kb's cause logic (`src/lib/kb/causes.ts`) over the reports merged into
#4471 and they do not share one cause. The desk merged on subject line alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), so two different bugs with the same
symptom landed in one ticket, and one fix was queued for both.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The table below is built from the export at render time; the counts are what the
data shows, not what the page said.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The export's pages overlap, so the same report can appear twice; the table counts each report id
once. The intake tag ("tagged as") is a guess from the reporter's browser locale and is wrong
often: it is not the cause. The cause follows the tenant: their locale, and the booking form they run.

## The two problems

**`parser`.** The shared date parser in `sched-prod` reads every date month first. Every tenant
on file writes the day first, so a booking on 7 April goes out as 4 July. Day and month swap
whenever the day is 1 to 12. It hits every channel: app, email and form. This is the bug the
queued fix is for.

**`hint`.** The `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. The tenant's people
type what the hint tells them, month first, and the form reads the value the tenant's way, day
first. Same symptom, different bug: it only hits booking-v3 tenants in day-first locales, and only
through the form. The parser fix does not touch it. Until now it had no ticket of its own.

## Tickets

One ticket per problem, in the desk's tracker. Each count is the number of reports in #4471 that
the ticket covers, computed from the export.

<SplitTickets ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## Read differently: the one-day moves

A few reports in the `parser` group describe a one-day shift, not a month flip: a Tuesday that
showed as Monday, the same meeting on different days in Lisbon and Toronto, an invite that
arrived before the booking. The desk noted them in `desk-notes.json`. By the kb's rule they are
counted where they are filed, by tenant, and footnoted under the table above. Engineering should
check them against the parser fix: a one-day move points at time zones, not at the parser.

## For the desk

- Subject line alone is not enough. Before merging a dates report, look up the tenant's form:
  `booking-v3` plus a day-first locale is `hint`, everything else day-first is `parser`.
  The [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) runs this check.
- Keep the counts in components. The old page typed "412 reports" into a paragraph; the number
  in the table above is computed and will follow the data when the desk keeps working.
- Decision 0001 accepted that same bugs end up in separate tickets. #4471 shows the other
  failure: different bugs in one ticket. A new decision record should replace it.

